  "description": "T1 � front garden - Ornamental cherry (Prunus species), multi-stem specimen, \r\nProposed works: Fell T1 to near ground level and remove all arising material. Grind \r\nout the stump/root plate as necessary to allow repair or rebuilding of the damaged \r\nboundary wall and to prevent continued conflict with the wall.\r\nIt is understood that the original cherry tree was felled by previous owners, but the \r\nstump and root system were not removed. The current tree has subsequently \r\nregenerated from the retained root system and is growing at approximately a 45\r\ndegree angle.\r\nThe tree is in an unsuitable, highly restricted position between the front boundary \r\nwalls. Its stem and root area are in direct contact with, or immediately adjacent to, the \r\nwall structure. There is already visible displacement, cracking and damage to the \r\nboundary wall beside the tree. As the cherry continues to mature, its stem girth and \r\nroot system are likely to create further pressure on the wall and potentially affect \r\nadjacent built structures. Removal is requested to prevent further damage and allow \r\nthe boundary wall to be properly repaired",
